WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.590
A world that’s lost its way needs a healer,
someone to patch up its wounds and tend to

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:07.819
its pain.

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:10.080
It needs a doctor.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.500
When day broke, and the sun turned from a
giver of life, the thing that wakes the rooster

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:20.900
and makes the crops grow, to an indiscriminate
killer wiping out all organic life forms.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.030
The world seemed truly lost.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:29.380
But one anomalous being made it his goal to
soothe the hurt, to make it safe to step into

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.289
the light once more.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:36.080
The Plague Doctor had done his best with the
limited resources afforded to him at the abandoned

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.500
Foundation site.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.680
The scientists had left behind all of their
equipment when the red sun came, when they

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.020
were transformed.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.450
He had appointed himself the Site Director,
willing to take up the mantle when no one

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.450
else would.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:54.920
He had assembled a brave, brilliant team of
fellow anomalies: the verbose Dr. Spanko,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.570
the eloquent adventurous Lord Blackwood, and
the charismatic but ravenous Fernand.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:05.030
There had, of course, been those who scoffed
at his vision, who did not share his noble

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.030
goal.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.840
The abominable Possessive Mask taunted him
persistently, trying its best to get under

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.840
his chitinous skin.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.119
But he did not have time to waste on such
trivial psychological games, and he ignored

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:21.119
its taunts to focus on The Work.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:26.020
It hadn't been easy, capturing one of the
infected specimens, the former human being

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.299
turned mass of oozing gelatinous flesh by
the unholy light in the sky.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:36.350
One had made its way into the abandoned facility,
sliding its way across the floor with an air

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.420
of confused malice.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.990
It wanted to hurt, but it didn't know where
it was, who it was, anymore.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.990
But it was frightened, the Plague Doctor could
tell.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.969
A good physician always knows, and can sense
the fear and pain of a suffering person.

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:57.609
It made his heart ache to see, and he knew
that there was only one thing to do: try to

00:01:57.609 --> 00:02:00.289
make this poor soul well again.

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:01.369
"Everyone!

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:04.930
Please assist me in escorting the patient
to my laboratory!"

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.170
The Doctor called out.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:12.540
"This was once a man, and I believe with our
combined intellect and resources, we can return

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.390
him to his former state!"

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:18.030
Fernand took a step toward the slimy creature,
licking his lips a bit.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.739
"Do you think I could have just a little bit
of it?

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:24.390
I'm so hungry, Doctor," he begged.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.390
"No!

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:30.760
No, it would go against my oath as a physician
to allow any more harm to come to this poor

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.760
fellow."

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.810
The Plague Doctor shook his head solemnly.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.070
Fernand pouted, but did not press the issue
further.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:42.220
"Now," The Doctor rubbed his gloved hands
together in anticipation of the next task.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.099
"It is imperative we contain our new friend
safely.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.620
If you would, please."

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.620
He gestured to several of his previous patients,
now reanimated and ready to aid him with his

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.620
research.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.780
The shuffling figures surrounded the blobby
entity, ushering it down the hall.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.940
Confused, lost, with no real sense of a plan
left in its mushy consciousness, the creature

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.510
followed where it was led.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.739
The group made it back to the Doctor's laboratory.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:08.739
"Cack!"

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:11.780
Shouted Dr. Spanko, from his perch atop a
nearby shelf.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.099
"Yes indeed!"

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:14.099
The Doctor replied.

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:18.980
"A standard operating table won't do for such
a special patient, I have nowhere to place

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.180
the restraints, you see.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.510
I will have to make do with the floor.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.530
Fernand, my bag if you please."

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.310
The giant rushed to his side, dropping the
bag at his feet.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.920
"If it dies, then can I eat it?"

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.959
He asked, shifting from one foot to the other
like a child asking a parent for a second

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:35.360
helping of ice cream.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:42.829
"If I am unable to save the patient, which
I do deem unlikely, then...yes, you may help

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:46.239
me dispose of the remains," the Doctor relented.

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:49.140
"But I hope it doesn't come to that."

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.180
He pressed a hand to his beak in deep thought
for a moment, before opening his bag and pulling

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.939
out a syringe filled with clear liquid.

00:03:55.939 --> 00:03:58.079
"To begin, we must sedate the patient."

00:03:58.079 --> 00:04:03.540
He had no way to find a vein, and so he plunged
the needle into the nearest section of the

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:07.000
creature's soft surface, injecting a dose
of sedative.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.670
Then, he waited.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.370
The oozing motion of the entity slowed and
stopped.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:15.959
It lay there on the ground, a still mound
of flesh save for the occasional expanding

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:19.329
and contracting motion, almost as if it was
breathing.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:20.329
Excellent.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:24.590
Now that there was no risk of the patient
fleeing the operating room mid-procedure,

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.210
he could truly begin.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:31.610
It was an arduous process that took hours
of effort, of taking small tissue samples,

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:35.310
attempting to make incisions only for the
flesh to fuse back together seconds after

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.360
the scalpel was taken away.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.250
This was truly an advanced illness, unlike
anything he had ever seen before.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:47.500
It was enough to make him question his abilities
as a doctor...but he shook the thought away.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.780
Self-pity never helped anyone.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.060
After about eight hours of continuous work,
he had a breakthrough.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:59.140
A solution he had created long ago, a thick
green liquid sealed in a dusty jar, had a

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:02.990
miraculous effect when dripped onto one of
the tissue samples.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:08.350
The melted flesh reconstituted, became solid
and human again.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.449
"Eureka!"

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:13.840
He cried out, unable to restrain the sudden
joy that leaped into his heart.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.310
This could be it.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:18.620
Very carefully, he filled a dropper with the
green liquid.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:22.080
If these initial trials had been successful,
then perhaps...

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.330
He couldn't finish the thought, best not to
get ahead of himself.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.449
He crossed to his patient, and slowly began
to pour the solution over the creature's viscous

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:31.449
surface.

00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:36.190
He watched as the flesh toughened, coming
together into a surface resembling human skin.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.840
It was working...it was working!

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:44.440
But then, the creature began to quiver, shaking
uncontrollably like a bowl of jelly in an

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.440
earthquake.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.539
The surface rippled, and the Doctor could
hear a high-pitched whine filling the room.

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:55.350
Then, with a wet pop, the patient exploded,
sending chunks of flesh splattering all over

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.990
the room, painting the walls and ceiling.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:03.039
The Doctor cried out in shock and horror,
and in spite of himself, fell to his knees

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:04.060
in despair.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.770
He had been so close, but still...he had failed.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.030
And who could say when he would find another
test subject?

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.569
If he would ever find a cure?

00:06:12.569 --> 00:06:17.840
"I'm afraid I do not know what to do now,"
the Doctor admitted.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.280
The next several days passed in a haze.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:26.740
The Doctor paced around his laboratory, mulling
over his possible mistakes again and again.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.020
He had rushed the process, he was certain
of that now.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:35.240
It was a novice mistake, the sort of thing
he might have done a century or two ago.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.400
How could he have been so foolish?

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.840
How could he have made that innocent pay the
price for his own hubris?

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.850
As the Doctor locked himself away in his mind
palace, Fernand occupied himself by practicing

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.889
his favorite songs.

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:52.789
Lord Blackwood rode on the massive man's shoulder
as he sang through the opera Don Giovanni.

00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:57.290
"I once saw a production of this at the Teatro
La Fenice in Venice!"

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.870
Lord Blackwood interjected, his rhinophores
twitching in delight at the memory.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.099
"Marvelous production, marvelous city.

00:07:03.099 --> 00:07:11.199
I was there hunting a rogue Tatzelwurm wreaking
havoc along the canals, I nearly lost my life

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:12.199
on that voyage."

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:15.820
"Would you all be quiet for once in your miserable
lives?"

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.580
A voice hissed from the shadows.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:23.169
There, in the doorway, its face fixed in a
frown, was the Possessive Mask.

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:28.039
Black slime dripped from its eyeholes, spilling
down onto the plastic mannequin body it had

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:29.909
taken hold of.

00:07:29.909 --> 00:07:35.889
"Listening to you both is worse than being
locked in that infernal box."

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:39.419
The mask looked around the room, searching
for something.

00:07:39.419 --> 00:07:42.580
"Where is the good doctor?"

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.889
It asked, voice dripping with disdain.

00:07:45.889 --> 00:07:50.580
"Still moping about, counting his failures?"

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.949
"Ignore him, my fine fellow."

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:55.030
Lord Blackwood whispered to Fernand.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:59.030
"Only those with weak constitutions and no
achievements of their own spend their days

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:00.050
dragging others down.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.540
When you have lived as long as I, you will
learn this."

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:03.540
"Careful, my Lord."

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:08.650
The Mask laughed a harsh, humorless laugh.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:15.820
"I'll stop by the kitchen and find some salt
to pour on you."

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.590
"If you wish to fight me, then challenge me
to a fair duel like a man!"

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.379
The colorful slug bellowed.

00:08:22.379 --> 00:08:25.139
Drawn by the sudden shouting, the Doctor walked
into the room.

00:08:25.139 --> 00:08:27.570
"What is all this commotion?"

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:30.280
"Oh, good!"

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:35.680
The Mask clapped its plastic hands together,
its face warping back into an eerie smile.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:41.909
"There you are, this has all been so dreadfully
boring.

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:48.260
I came to see the remnants of your greatest
shame, are there still bloodstains on the

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.960
floor in your pathetic little laboratory?"

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.430
"You are a villain," the Doctor seethed.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.890
Uncomfortable with the air of conflict in
the room, Fernand and Lord Blackwood quickly

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:03.820
exited, to find another space where they could
sing and share stories in peace.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:10.600
"I simply speak the truths no one wants to
hear!"

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.920
The Mask crossed to the Doctor's side with
a series of light, dance-like steps that made

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.620
the mannequin body creak.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:23.550
"In fact, I have quite a few truths to share
today.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.800
I've been outside, you see.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:30.459
Whatever's become of the sun only affects
organic beings, and so..."

00:09:30.459 --> 00:09:33.950
He gestured from his ceramic face to his plastic
body.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:38.950
"I am quite safe from its rays."

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.100
"You've been outside?"

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.540
The Doctor couldn't keep the curiosity out
of his voice.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.610
He was a scientist, after all.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:46.970
"Why yes.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:51.079
Would you like to know what I've seen?"

00:09:51.079 --> 00:09:55.430
Black slime dripped from the Mask's mouth,
pooling on the floor with a sizzling sound.

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:59.470
"I'm in no mood for tricks," the Doctor warned.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.330
The Mask held up his hands in mock surrender.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.350
"No tricks here, Doctor.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:12.720
But if you'd rather take your chances outside
and see for yourself, I can take my leave

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:13.720
now..."

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:14.720
"No!"

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:15.720
The Doctor shook his head.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.720
"Please.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:17.720
Do tell me."

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:23.800
"It is so much worse than you can even imagine."

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:27.190
The Mask's words were bleak, but its tone
was gleeful.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:32.690
"Everywhere you look out there, the light
has made monsters.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:40.741
Humans, dogs, cats, mice, the wild beasts
of the forest, all melted down into creatures

00:10:40.741 --> 00:10:43.080
you would not even recognize.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.670
But that isn't all!

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.860
No, that is not all.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:54.480
There are massive beasts, ten feet tall or
more, made from dozens and dozens of the creatures

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.630
coming together.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:11:03.070
They fuse and meld into one giant entity,
roving the streets in search of more and more

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:09.399
bodies to add to the pile, an oozing, gaping
maw of hunger and hate that seeks only to

00:11:09.399 --> 00:11:11.910
consume and destroy.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:17.050
It calls out to surviving humans in the voices
of their fallen loved ones, tugs at their

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:23.040
heartstrings to lure them out of their hiding
places, and then...It wraps around them with

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:28.579
fleshy tentacles, pulling them in until they
are no more.

00:11:28.579 --> 00:11:30.570
Just another part of the monster.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:34.250
Oh, Doctor...it's a terror.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.019
It's an abomination.

00:11:37.019 --> 00:11:41.589
I could watch it all day."

00:11:41.589 --> 00:11:46.399
The Doctor wanted to believe the Mask was
lying, that it was trying to torment him with

00:11:46.399 --> 00:11:52.580
awful fabrications, but after all he had seen
so far...he knew that its words were true.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.930
"Get out of my sight," He said.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:57.220
"Or what?"

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:00.209
The Mask stared him down with its unmoving
smile.

00:12:00.209 --> 00:12:03.740
"I've seen what you do to your hosts, you
know.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:08.050
Your body won't last forever," the Doctor
growled.

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:09.529
"True.

00:12:09.529 --> 00:12:16.920
Maybe next, I'll take yours."

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:22.529
The Mask laughed a long, dark laugh of something
ancient and evil, then it turned and walked

00:12:22.529 --> 00:12:25.199
out the door, leaving the Doctor alone.

00:12:25.199 --> 00:12:27.850
He spent so much of his time that way, lately.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.481
His assistants were preoccupied, his former
patients provided no real company, and so

00:12:32.481 --> 00:12:36.510
he did what he did best: carry on in solitude.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:41.399
He couldn't be sure how long he stood there
in silence, thinking of what the Mask told

00:12:41.399 --> 00:12:42.399
him.

00:12:42.399 --> 00:12:47.019
He knew it was dangerous outside, knew he
was up against powerful destructive forces,

00:12:47.019 --> 00:12:50.070
but it was even worse than he had thought.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.839
What if the world was truly doomed?

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:58.200
What if this was how it all ended, not with
a bang, but with a great melting?

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:02.280
Suddenly, the Doctor heard a sound he hadn't
heard since the sun turned wrong.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.440
A scream.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:05.290
A human scream.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.290
Could it be?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.430
He had to see for himself.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:11.790
He grabbed his bag of tools and rushed down
the hall, his robes fluttering behind him.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:12.940
There it was, again!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.640
A different human voice, screaming in terror.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.820
As he grew closer to the sound, he could hear
footsteps, various other voices overlapping

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:20.820
with each other.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:26.130
He rounded a corner, and there they were:
a group of five humans, wrapped in tattered

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:29.130
clothes, dirty and exhausted.

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.790
Behind them was the entrance to what looked
like a tunnel.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.690
Somehow they had found a secret passage, and
made their way inside!

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:37.460
Then, he saw what had made them scream.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:42.540
Clearly, these people were afraid, and unaccustomed
to the sight of a man of Fernand's stature.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:45.959
Especially when that man was drooling and
staring at them with hunger in his eyes.

00:13:45.959 --> 00:13:48.459
He would have to diffuse the situation quickly.

00:13:48.459 --> 00:13:49.459
"Hello!

00:13:49.459 --> 00:13:50.459
Welcome!

00:13:50.459 --> 00:13:54.240
We mean you no harm, strangers!" he stepped
between Fernand and the humans.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:57.640
A man at the front of the group brandished
a firearm, pointing the barrel directly at

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:58.940
the Doctor's beak.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.380
"Please, sir, there is no need for violence."

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.290
"What are you?"

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.519
The man stammered.

00:14:04.519 --> 00:14:06.850
The other members of his party cowered behind
him.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:09.880
"An ally, if you will permit me to be.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:14.661
I am a physician, you see, working on a cure
for the condition that plagues the world."

00:14:14.661 --> 00:14:17.060
With a shaking hand, the man slowly lowered
his gun.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.470
He did not put it away, though.

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:22.420
"You've figured out a cure for those...things?"

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:26.040
"I am in the process of developing it.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.440
So far, I have not been successful, but perhaps
with your help?"

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:33.240
"How do we know we can trust you?"

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:34.240
The man demanded.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.630
"How am I supposed to know you're not a part
of this?"

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.990
"Do you know who this man is?!"

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:40.320
Fernand bellowed.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:46.660
"This is Doctor John Watson, and I am Detective
Sherlock Holmes, the greatest investigator

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.010
in the world.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.029
There isn't a case we can't solve!"

00:14:50.029 --> 00:14:53.519
The man looked at a woman next to him, and
the two shared a wide-eyed glance.

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:55.700
"This guy's crazy..."

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:56.839
He whispered furtively.

00:14:56.839 --> 00:15:02.040
"Put your weapon away, and we can speak more
calmly," the Doctor proposed.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:07.009
At this inopportune moment, a few of his revived
patients shambled into view, and the man screamed

00:15:07.009 --> 00:15:08.009
again.

00:15:08.009 --> 00:15:11.330
This time, he fired his weapon, shooting at
one of the walking corpses.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:14.420
The bullets ricocheted off the walls, and
several of the patients were hit.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.420
"Please!

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:16.420
Stop!"

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:19.410
With no other option, the Doctor grabbed the
man's arm, hoping to get ahold of the weapon

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.350
and end the potential bloodshed.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:25.530
As soon as his gloved hand made contact, the
man went limp and dropped to the ground with

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.530
a hard thud.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.949
The woman next to him pulled him into her
arms, checking his pulse.

00:15:29.949 --> 00:15:31.190
"He's dead!"

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.550
She shrieked, tears streaming down her face.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:37.120
"I...I am so sorry, my Lady, I did not intend..."

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.090
She grabbed the man's gun and trained it on
the Doctor once more.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.410
"You killed him!"

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:42.410
She cried.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:45.699
The other survivors were too shaken to speak,
to move.

00:15:45.699 --> 00:15:49.680
One of them had his back turned to the group,
and was staring into the darkness of the tunnel

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:50.680
behind him.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.709
Whatever he was looking at, it was worse than
the chaos unfolding.

00:15:53.709 --> 00:15:59.160
But no one noticed the beige flesh tentacle
snaking along the ground until it was too

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.160
late.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.829
Until it had grabbed ahold of the man's ankle
and dragged him into the tunnel with a shriek

00:16:03.829 --> 00:16:06.149
of pure, unadulterated terror.

00:16:06.149 --> 00:16:10.910
The woman nearly dropped her gun at the sound,
whirling around to see what had happened.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:15.880
Deep in the tunnel, the scream warped into
a wet gurgling sound, and then there was silence

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.579
for a long moment.

00:16:17.579 --> 00:16:19.320
But then, something worse.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:25.980
A gooey, slimy sound, the sound of something
enormous, something soft and fleshy, making

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.209
its way through the tunnel and toward the
group.

00:16:29.209 --> 00:16:33.440
Another tentacle curled around the edge of
the opening, then another joined it.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:38.779
Something emerged that might have once been
a hand, but had melted into something unrecognizable.

00:16:38.779 --> 00:16:43.490
The monster emerged piece by piece, until
the Doctor could see the entire thing.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:48.459
It looked like a heap of people, dozens of
them, clambering on top of each other, wrapping

00:16:48.459 --> 00:16:53.639
their limbs together until their flesh and
insides emptied out and fused into a shapeless

00:16:53.639 --> 00:16:54.639
mass.

00:16:54.639 --> 00:16:59.209
It moved a bit like a giant slug, slimy and
slow, but it seemed to know it could take

00:16:59.209 --> 00:17:00.399
its time.

00:17:00.399 --> 00:17:04.710
As the survivors scrambled back away from
it, Fernand and the Doctor taking a few steps

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:08.520
back of their own, the sound of human voices
filled the room.

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:13.120
There were unintelligible whispers, the soft
giggle of a child, a woman weeping.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.730
"Come and be with us..."

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:17.110
A little boy's voice broke through the cacophony.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:20.480
"Mommy...I miss you, don't you miss me?"

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:23.300
The woman with the gun let out a broken sob.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:24.300
"Billy?"

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.300
She sniffled.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.300
"It's me, mommy..."

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:30.470
The innocent voice continued, emanating from
somewhere deep inside the monstrous mass that

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:34.320
crept along the ground, swelling and grasping
with its ropy tentacles.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.260
"Come play with me, outside...

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.950
All you have to do is come outside..."

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:43.500
"Madam, the creature is not who it claims
to be," the Doctor spoke up, and it seemed

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.540
to shake the woman out of a trance.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:50.570
"You're not my son," she hissed, squeezing
the trigger and firing at the monster.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:55.370
The bullet made contact with a wet, useless
slap, and disappeared into the roving pile

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.380
of the fallen.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.780
She fired again, and again, but the monster
did not stop.

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.880
It didn't even slow down.

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:05.920
It lashed out with a tentacle that wrapped
around her throat in a single fluid motion,

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.670
and snapped her neck with a crack.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:13.650
She fell to the ground, and the tentacle pulled
her into its depths until she was no longer

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:14.650
visible.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:18.610
She hadn't been taken by the sun, not yet,
but she was still lost.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:23.080
The rest of the survivors followed, their
screams silenced one by one.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.510
The Doctor felt the same overwhelming sense
of hopelessness wash over him, the same shadow

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:30.920
that had passed over him when he lost the
last patient.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.071
What could he do?

00:18:32.071 --> 00:18:36.070
He was one physician against an overpowering
force of destruction.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:40.820
Perhaps he could touch it, and it would fall
dead like so many other organisms before?

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:42.190
But what if it didn't?

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:46.310
What if instead it wrapped around his body
and squeezed the life from him?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:50.710
What if it carried him out into that cursed
sunlight and he melted away like the others?

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:54.270
He had to make a decision, because the beast
was advancing toward him.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.270
"Doctor!"

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:56.280
Fernand shouted.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.440
"It's going to destroy our facility!"

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:02.600
Indeed, the creature was flailing its appendages
around, beating against the walls and trying

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:07.560
to tear down steel and plaster, break down
the shelter until they too were exposed to

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:08.720
the deadly light.

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:12.730
"I'm afraid this may be the end, my friend,"
the Doctor lamented.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:15.880
"I can see no hope for us now."

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.880
"No."

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:17.880
Fernand shook his head.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.540
"Let me save us.

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:21.260
Let me lead it back outside."

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.680
"You'll be taken!"

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.680
The Doctor cried.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.680
"Perhaps not!

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:27.780
I am a magnificent specimen, after all.

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:33.600
I believe I can withstand the sun, and return
to continue our work together," Fernand scooped

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:37.950
a sleeping Lord Blackwood from his shoulder
and placed him gingerly on a nearby shelf.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.970
"Thank you for your company."

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.590
Then he turned back to the Doctor.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.980
"And thank you for my freedom.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:44.980
And your friendship.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:48.000
It has been an honor."

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.470
Before the Doctor could protest, Fernand was
running, his thunderous steps pounding the

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.790
earth as he led the monster in a chase.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:58.590
It took the bait, following this new, large
target back outside.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:02.980
He sealed off the tunnel behind them, ensuring
the beast would not return the way it came.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:07.870
He wanted to believe Fernand's bravado, to
think that the behemoth of a man had survived

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:08.870
outside.

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:13.960
But that night, he saw the great beast ooze
past a window, and could make out that familiar

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.830
wide, toothy grin protruding from its side.

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:21.030
Just like that, the greatest assistant he
had ever had was lost.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:25.480
"Thank you for your service, my friend," He
whispered to himself.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:30.290
"I solemnly swear to you, your death shall
not be in vain..."

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:37.000
Now go check out “When Day Breaks SCP-049”
and “When Day Breaks SCP-096” for more

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.360
terrifying tales from the world of When Day
Breaks!

